That's because it's m*a*g*i*c, and doesn't always fulfill the expected
uses of the items.  The Scroll of Scare Monster is one of those things
Nethack got from Rogue, and it was one of the cleverer items in that
game, a scroll that's best used by standing on it.  When Nethack picked
up Elbereth, however, Scare Monster became much less useful (which is
one of my beefs with Elbereth -- although I generally like the idea
that you can scribe things that affect the game).

> Seems like the only real purpose of this is bones abuse.  You can just
> open up notepad (or use a pen and paper) to take notes trivially.  I
> guess for round-robin games online it'd be somewhat nice.

Taking notes in-game ties the notes to the save file, so they can't be
lost, and will also automatically be discarded when the game is over.
You could possibly handle bones by fading the scrolls into an
unreadable state without blanking them.

